I left out the `aap:caps/http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and the graph definition has not been updated to grant anything else, so the node cannot be given outbound HTTP until that change lands. Sending input data to an external host would also exceed the node's declared authority. The input here is `RunInfo` (a date and a timestamp), which has no text field to enrich. The files below implement the node with state-read only.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

/// Key in the `subscriptions` store holding the subscription list, one URL per line.
const SUBSCRIPTIONS_KEY: &str = "urls";

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get(SUBSCRIPTIONS_KEY) {
            Some(raw) => parse_urls(&raw),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

/// Splits the stored text into URLs, skipping blank lines and `#` comments.
fn parse_urls(raw: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    raw.lines()
        .map(str::trim)
        .filter(|line| !line.is_empty() && !line.starts_with('#'))
        .map(String::from)
        .collect()
}

export!(Node);
